Proposed php-vm changes for ext/zend_test (crates/php-ext-zendtest), against 04c037a.
Apply with `git apply` from the repository root, then enable the binding
side by adding `features = ["vm-hooks"]` to the php-ext-zendtest line of
crates/php-cli/Cargo.toml.

1. Observer API (new crates/php-vm/src/observer.rs; hooks in call.rs,
   exec.rs, include.rs, generator.rs; Frame::observed; Vm::observer):
   `Vm::set_observer(ObserverHooks { init, begin, end, internal_enter,
   internal_leave })` and `Vm::current_exception()`, re-exported from
   php_vm::ext together with `ObservedFrame`. `init` runs once per
   function/file (zend_observer_fcall_init), `begin`/`end` around every
   user call, native call (before zpp / after the handler), main script,
   include/eval and generator resumption (end at each yield with the
   yielded value); unwinding ends frames with `None` and the exception
   available through `current_exception()`; bailout/exit ends all
   observed frames (zend_observer_fcall_end_all). Hook code is never
   observed itself. `internal_enter`/`internal_leave` wrap every native
   body (zend_execute_internal override). The VM-only
   `Generator::__destruct` frame is not reported.
2. Internal attribute registry (compiler/attrs.rs, reflection/attribute.rs,
   ext.rs): `ModuleBuilder::internal_attribute(class, flags, validator)`
   (zend_mark_internal_attribute): compile-time target/repeat checks and
   a validator for extension attribute classes, and
   ReflectionAttribute::newInstance() accepting them.
3. `Vm::call_function` (native code calling a native helper by name, e.g.
   realpath() from SoapClient) is not observed: it is a C call in php-src.

Measured on 3be3cf4 (4 Nov 2026) with these applied: ext/zend_test/tests
105/168 (64 without), the zend_test-gated tests elsewhere 104/136 (99
without).

